      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "gpc:cc-tou-oa-2026-06-01",
        "@type": "urpx:CoverageClaim",
        "urpx:completenessResult": {
          "@id": "urpx:partial"
        },
        "urpx:selfContained": true,
        "urpx:explainedBy": {
          "@type": "urpx:Evaluation",
          "@id": "gpc:cc-tou-oa-2026-06-01-evaluation",
          "urpx:evaluationKind": {
            "@id": "urpx:coverageEvaluation"
          },
          "urpx:description": "This filing does not carry everything its source document states. 4 parts are deferred, listed here in the same words as the filing's tariff.toml [modeling].deferrals so the two records cannot drift. (1) Municipal Franchise Fee base. MFF-11 applies to the total revenues of each bill, which include the ECCR-15 and DSM-R-16 amounts. Its multiplier Prices here are based on the energy-and-fuel subtotal and on the Basic Service Charge Price, not on the ECCR and DSM-R multiplier Prices, so the franchise fee on those two amounts, about 0.44 percent of the base bill inside city limits, is not carried. (2) Minimum Monthly Bill. The sheet sets it at the Basic Service Charge plus ECCR, DSM-R and the Municipal Franchise Fee, and no Price carries it. Every energy and fuel price here is positive, so a bill on these prices alone is never below it. (3) Term of Contract. The sheet requires a customer to remain on TOU-OA for twelve months from the contract date, renewed automatically each year unless terminated with 30 days' notice before the anniversary. Nothing is priced by it and it is not carried. (4) Fuel Cost Recovery voltage levels. TOU-FCR-TP-5 also prices Primary Distribution and Transmission customers. Only the Secondary Distribution rates are carried, as Prices with no condition, so they apply to every customer on the schedule.",
          "urpx:evaluatedOn": "2026-10-17T00:00:00"
        }
      }
    }
